  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a plan, but haven't changed any code, since plan mode is on. I also couldn't find the tool that formally submits a plan for approval, so I'm putting it here instead.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/click/core.py:392`, a subcommand's context gets the parent's entire `default_map` instead of the part filed under the subcommand's name. A map like `{\"sub\": {\"name\": \"from-map\"}}` should give the `sub` command its `--name` default. Instead, `sub` looks for `\"name\"` at the top level, doesn't find it, and the default is ignored.\n\n**Proposed fix (one line):**\n```python\ndefault_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)\n```\nThis matches how upstream Click does it. A subcommand with no entry in the map gets no defaults from it.\n\n**Test:** I'd add a test to `tests/test_defaults.py` that checks three things:\n- A subcommand picks up its default from the nested map.\n- A subcommand two levels down (`{\"a\": {\"b\": {...}}}`) also works.\n- A top-level key with the same name doesn't leak into the subcommand.\n\n**To verify:** run `python -m pytest tests -q`. The new test and the existing nested-map test at `test_defaults.py:447` should both pass.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-breezy-blossom.md`. Should I go ahead and make the change?",
